  "body": "Follow-up of #3466 (item 3 of that issue). The fix for #3466 is in the shipped posts only.\n\n## What the code does\n- The Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts now command the rotaries back to zero at the start of a section that follows a tilted section (PR for #3466).\n- Tormach PathPilot and Mach4 already do this.\n- A post script that a user loads (`PostRef::File`) has no such law. If it does not state the return, an upright operation after a tilted operation cuts with the rotaries still tilted. No check stops it.\n\n## Necessary work\n1. A manifest flag (for example `uprightAfterTilt = true`) that says: the script commands the rotaries to zero, at a safe height, at the start of each section that follows a tilted section.\n2. The post engine (or the app post gate) refuses, by name, a program with an upright section after a tilted section when the script does not declare the flag.\n3. Each shipped post that writes tilted moves declares the flag. Each such post has a posting test of the real order (see `crates/post/tests/upright_after_tilt.rs`).\n4. A Mach4 pin in that test file (the AC trunnion fixture of `mach4_trunnion.rs` must move to a shared helper first).\n\nRefs #3466\n",
